course: dictionary
lesson: 8459
title: Salad: a cold dish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A salad is a cold dish, usually made of mixed vegetables like lettuce, tomato and cucumber, often with a dressing poured over it. Notice that it is served cold, so it is not a hot meal like soup.
explain: Salads can be more than vegetables. A fruit salad is a mix of cut-up fruit, and a salad can also have pasta, rice, eggs, cheese or meat in it. «Toad hunts out cold chicken, trifle and lobster salad» shows a salad with seafood in it, so the clue is the list of other foods around the word.
explain: Context helps you here. «Shake a bottle of salad dressing» tells you that dressing is something you pour on a salad, and the word salad is the thing it goes with.
fact: A salad is a cold dish of mixed vegetables, like lettuce, tomato and cucumber, often with a dressing.
fact: A fruit salad is a mix of cut-up fruit.
fact: Salads can also have pasta, rice, eggs, cheese or meat in them.
fact: Salads give vitamins and fibre, so they are part of a balanced diet.
fact: Before making a salad, wash the vegetables, and use a knife carefully when you cut them.
exercise: Mia's bowl had lettuce, tomato and cucumber, with dressing on top. What kind of dish is it? | A sandwich | *A salad | A pudding | A hot soup
exercise: Which of these is a fruit salad? | Cooked rice in a pot | *Cut-up melon, grapes and kiwi in a bowl | Lettuce, tomato and cucumber in a bowl | Cold chicken on a plate
exercise: «Toad hunts out cold chicken, trifle and lobster salad.» Find and copy one food in this sentence that is a salad. | trifle | chicken | cold | *lobster salad
test: «Toad hunts out cold chicken, trifle and lobster salad.» Lobster salad is a salad with what in it? | *Seafood, like lobster | Only lettuce | Only cheese | Only fruit
test: Why are salads good for you? | They are full of sugar | They make you sleepy | *They give vitamins and fibre | They have no vegetables in them
exam: Before you make a salad, what should you do with the vegetables? | Throw them away | Cook them for an hour | Paint them | *Wash them
